# WHAT A PLAUSIBLE EDIT COULD BREAK HERE: this Operator relays commands to machines on
# patrons' own networks and keeps pictures of their screens. Review with that in mind:
# - the proof gates (runtime.require_caller_proof on pair_agent, agent_status,
#   forget_display) — dropping one lets anyone who knows an npub see or remove its displays;
# - snapshot.parse, the untrusted-input check on everything an agent sends back;
# - store.keep_latest, which must refuse to store a picture it cannot encrypt, and its AAD
#   binding a picture to its display;
# - agent secrets living only in the patron credential vault, never in a column;
# - forget_display's cascade, which must leave nothing of a forgotten display behind.
